⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
288 calories 32g protein (for the entire pint, including toppings and mix-ins)
Oat of this Swirled Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 100 recipes like this one!

- 1 Vanilla Protein Shake + 25g @Lakanto Brown Monk Fruit sweetener
— or 400g Fat Free High Protein Milk + 40-45g Brown Monk Fruit sweetener
- 1g (¼ tsp) butter extract
- 1g (¼ tsp) salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 15g chocolate chips + 2g coconut oil
🍫Chocolate chip hack:
Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 15g of chocolate with 2g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips.
- ½ of a @MadeGoodFoods Cinnamon Bun Baked Oat bar (or similar cookie swirl replacement - about 60 cal)
288 cal 21g C, 11g F, 32g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting
5. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the melted chocolate
6. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
7. Crumble the bar on top

